issue.body:
Fixes [GIT-1802](https://linear.app/activepieces/issue/GIT-1802)
Closes #15054

## Problem
1. The trigger node of every flow (including the `Select Trigger` placeholder) and every node in a run's read-only builder rendered `role="button" aria-disabled="true"`, while clicking it still opens the step.
2. Screen readers announce these nodes as dimmed, and Playwright refuses a normal click ("element is not enabled", 10s timeout).

## Fix
- `packages/web/src/app/builder/flow-canvas/nodes/step-node/index.tsx`: drop `aria-disabled` from the `useDraggable` attributes before spreading them on the clickable node. dnd-kit sets it from `disabled: isTrigger || readonly`, which means "not draggable", not "not clickable". `role`, `tabIndex`, `aria-roledescription` and the drag listeners are unchanged.

## Verification
- Regression test `packages/web/test/app/builder/flow-canvas/nodes/step-node/index.test.tsx` (4 cases: editor trigger, editor action, read-only trigger, read-only action). Red-first: 4/4 fail on the base commit, 4/4 pass with the fix.
- Lint: `eslint` clean on both changed files (web config). A full local `npm run lint-dev` did not finish because the dev box ran out of headroom. The CI lint job on this PR is the full gate.
- Code review: 7 findings, 1 applied (the test no longer locks in `aria-roledescription` on non-draggable nodes). The rest are pre-existing or outside this ticket and are listed under Non-happy scenarios.
- Security review: the `/security-review` skill could not run in this session; manual review of the diff found nothing (no auth, input, network or data handling touched).
- Visual: real dev stack (PGLite), driven with Playwright. New flow `Select Trigger` node and a failed run's read-only builder (trigger node), before and after. Screenshots in the Visual verification comment.
- Other affected paths: checked - `note-node` and `components/ui/sortable.tsx` also use dnd-kit but never pass `disabled`, so they never emit `aria-disabled="true"`.
- Repro: Playwright `locator.click()` on the node against the running app. Base refuses after 10s, fix clicks in under 300 ms and opens the step. Full steps in the Reproduction block.

### Breaking change?

- [x] no, reviewed, not breaking
- [ ] yes, technical (removed/renamed API field or endpoint, dropped column, new required field, removed/required env var)
- [ ] yes, functional (default/limit/behaviour change, new self-hosted setup step)

### Security impact?

- [x] no, reviewed, no security impact
- [ ] yes, security-sensitive (call out the risk and mitigation in the description above)

<details>
<summary>Plan & reasoning</summary>

## Plan
- Acted on the internal triage comment on the ticket (VERIFIED, root cause in `step-node/index.tsx`).
- Strip `aria-disabled` at the one spread site. Footprint estimate: 1 file, ~3 lines. Actual: 1 file, +5/-1.

## Non-happy scenarios considered
- Draggable action node in the editor: dnd-kit used to emit `aria-disabled="false"`. Now the attribute is absent, which means the same thing to assistive tech. Drag listeners unchanged.
- Read-only builder: nodes stay clickable (`onClick` is unconditional and opens the step's run output), so reporting them as enabled is correct.
- Keyboard: no Enter/Space handler on the node, and no `KeyboardSensor` in `flow-drag-layer.tsx`. The editable action nodes already worked this way before this PR. Out of scope, a follow-up.
- Non-draggable nodes still carry dnd-kit's `aria-roledescription="draggable"` and `aria-describedby` drag hint. The ticket asks to keep them. Not asserted by the test, so a follow-up can drop them.
- Node is a clickable `div` with a borrowed `role="button"`, not a real `<button>`. Converting it is a layout change, so it is out of scope.
- Piece selector open: dnd attributes are already suppressed (`stepNodeDivAttributes = {}`). Unchanged.

## Alternatives rejected
- Moving drag attributes to a separate drag handle: restructures the node's layout for an attribute bug.
- `aria-disabled={undefined}` after the spread: depends on prop order, which is easy to break silently.
- Shared wrapper around `useDraggable`: only one caller passes `disabled`.
</details>

<details>
<summary>Reproduction</summary>

## Environment
- `npm run dev` on `main` at the PR's base commit, `AP_DB_TYPE=PGLITE`, `AP_QUEUE_MODE=MEMORY`, `AP_DEV_PIECES="google-sheets,store,webhook"`. Signed in as the dev seed user (`dev@ap.com`).
- Flow A: new empty flow (only the `Select Trigger` placeholder).
- Flow B: `Catch Webhook` trigger plus a Code step, published, enabled, called once through `/api/v1/webhooks/<flowId>/sync` to produce a run. Opened at `/projects/<projectId>/runs/<runId>` (read-only builder).

## Harness
`node-click-check.mjs`, run from the repo root (it imports `@playwright/test` from the root `node_modules`):

```js
import { chromium } from '@playwright/test';

const baseUrl = process.env.BASE_URL ?? 'http://localhost:4200';
const pagePath = process.env.PAGE_PATH;
const stepName = process.env.STEP_NAME ?? 'trigger';
const shot = process.env.SHOT ?? '/tmp/node-click-check.png';

const browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: '/usr/bin/google-chrome' });
const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1440, height: 900 } });
await page.addInitScript(() => {
  const hideDevOverlay = () => {
    const style = document.createElement('style');
    style.textContent = 'vite-plugin-checker-error-overlay{display:none!important}';
    document.documentElement.appendChild(style);
  };
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', hideDevOverlay);
  } else {
    hideDevOverlay();
  }
});
await page.goto(`${baseUrl}/sign-in`);
await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('dev@ap.com');
await page.getByLabel('Password').fill('12345678');
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' }).click();
await page.waitForURL('**/projects/**');
await page.goto(`${baseUrl}${pagePath}`);
const node = page.locator(`[data-step-context-menu="${stepName}"]`);
await node.waitFor();
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
const attrs = await node.evaluate((el) =>
  Object.fromEntries(
    ['role', 'tabindex', 'aria-disabled', 'aria-roledescription'].map((n) => [n, el.getAttribute(n)]),
  ),
);
console.log('node attributes', JSON.stringify(attrs));
console.log('getByRole(button).isEnabled', await node.isEnabled());
const started = Date.now();
try {
  await node.click({ timeout: 10000 });
  console.log(`normal click: OK after ${Date.now() - started} ms`);
} catch (e) {
  console.log(`normal click: REFUSED after ${Date.now() - started} ms: ${e.message.split('\n').find((l) => l.includes('not enabled')) ?? e.message.split('\n')[0]}`);
}
await page.waitForTimeout(1500);
console.log('sidebar/dialog open', await page.locator('[role=dialog], [data-testid=right-sidebar], aside').count());
await page.screenshot({ path: shot });
await browser.close();
```

Run: `PAGE_PATH=/projects/<projectId>/flows/<flowId> node node-click-check.mjs` (Flow A), `PAGE_PATH=/projects/<projectId>/runs/<runId> STEP_NAME=trigger node node-click-check.mjs` (Flow B). The init script only hides the dev-mode type-checker overlay, which otherwise covers the page.

## Trigger
A default Playwright `locator.click()` on `[data-step-context-menu="<step>"]`. It waits until the element is enabled, which is exactly what `aria-disabled="true"` fails.

## Results
| Surface | Base | Fix |
| -- | -- | -- |
| New flow, `Select Trigger` node | `aria-disabled="true"`, `isEnabled false`, click REFUSED after 10002 ms | no `aria-disabled`, `isEnabled true`, click OK in 175 ms |
| Run view, trigger node | `aria-disabled="true"`, click REFUSED after 10003 ms, sidebar stays on the failed step | no `aria-disabled`, click OK in 294 ms, sidebar switches to `1. Catch Webhook` |
| Run view, action node | `aria-disabled="true"`, click REFUSED after 10003 ms | no `aria-disabled`, click OK in 106 ms |
</details>
